{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Monotone.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":24,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.hump_is_neither","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.hump_is_neither","kind":"theorem","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L326-L331","doc":"Negative control: the blocking above is a statement about *affine* paths\nonly, and is not vacuous — `hump` from `Sharpness` is a law the affine theorems\ngenuinely do not cover, since it is neither monotone nor antitone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.linear_functional_on_affine_path_blocks_sign_mixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.linear_functional_on_affine_path_blocks_sign_mixed","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L312-L324","doc":"**The structural statement.**  A linear interface functional, evaluated along\n*any* affine path in the algebra, cannot reach the sign-mixed pattern — for\neither sign of the slope, and without computing a single bond value.\n\nThis is why the corpus's `μ = z + d` is blocked, and it locates the escape\nprecisely: it must leave the **affine path**, not merely the affine formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.linear_along_affine_path","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.linear_along_affine_path","kind":"theorem","line":303,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L303-L310","doc":"**A linear functional evaluated along an affine path is affine in the path\nparameter.**  `φ` here stands for `x ↦ tr_M(W·x)` at fixed `W`, which is linear\nbecause the Markov trace is.  Pure ring algebra — the order instances are\n`omit`ted because the statement genuinely does not use them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.affine_blocks_sign_mixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.affine_blocks_sign_mixed","kind":"theorem","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L291-L300","doc":"**No affine interface law reaches the sign-mixed pattern, whatever the sign\nof its slope.**  This subsumes `PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed`'s `μ = z + d` as\nthe case `a = z`, `b = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.affine_monotone_or_antitone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.affine_monotone_or_antitone","kind":"theorem","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L277-L289","doc":"**An affine law is monotone or antitone**, according to the sign of its\nslope.  So both blocking theorems are available and neither sign escapes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.signMixed_impossible_of_antitone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.signMixed_impossible_of_antitone","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L270-L275","doc":"And the corresponding sign-mixed corollary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.pn_not_strict_max_of_antitone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.pn_not_strict_max_of_antitone","kind":"theorem","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L261-L268","doc":"The antitone half of the pn exclusion, which `pn_not_strict_max_of_monotone`\ndoes not cover: a *decreasing* interface law blocks the pattern just as a\nincreasing one does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.between_iff_combo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.between_iff_combo","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L205-L212","doc":"**The averaging hypothesis is exactly betweenness.** No weaker condition is\nhiding inside it, so unlike convexity and affineness this one admits no\nsharpening — `qou-q8vl`'s first escape is stated at full strength already. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.between_of_combo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.between_of_combo","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L200-L203","doc":"**And a weight gives betweenness**, so the two hypotheses coincide. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.combo_of_between","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.combo_of_between","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L188-L198","doc":"**Betweenness gives a weight.** Any value strictly between two others is a\nstrict convex combination of them, with the weight read off explicitly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.nonmonotone_escape_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.nonmonotone_escape_exists","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L158-L163","doc":"Stated as the escape it is: there exists an interface law under which the\nmiddle letter is the strict maximum, and it is necessarily non-monotone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.hump_realises_strict_max","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.hump_realises_strict_max","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L151-L156","doc":"**The narrowing is sharp.** A non-monotone law *does* put the middle strictly\nabove both endpoints — so monotonicity is exactly the invariant that blocks the\npattern, not a sufficient condition standing in for something weaker. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.hump_not_antitone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.hump_not_antitone","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L144-L149","doc":"Nor antitone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.hump_not_monotone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.hump_not_monotone","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L137-L142","doc":"It is not monotone: it rises then falls. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.hump_values","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.hump_values","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L134-L135","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.hump","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.hump","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L125-L131","doc":"A non-monotone interface law: the downward parabola `f d = 1 − (d − 1)²`,\npeaking at the midpoint of `[0, 2]`.\n\nStated over a generic ordered field, not `ℝ`: nothing archimedean is used — no\n`Real.sqrt`, no `rpow`, no transcendental — so §7c keeps it on the generic side\nof the substrate/archimedean wall along with the rest of this file. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.signMixed_impossible_of_monotone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.signMixed_impossible_of_monotone","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L110-L117","doc":"**Corollary — the pattern is unreachable under any monotone law.** So\nabandoning affineness, on its own, buys nothing: the construction is dead before\nany bond value is computed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.signMixedPattern","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.signMixedPattern","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L106-L108","doc":"The required pattern, as `qou-q8vl` states it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.pn_not_strict_max_of_monotone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.pn_not_strict_max_of_monotone","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L95-L104","doc":"**The sharpened exclusion.** For *any* monotone interface law `f` — affine or\nnot — a pn letter that is a strict convex combination of the like-pair letters\ncannot produce a pn bond factor that strictly exceeds both like-pair factors.\n\n`PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed.pn_not_strict_max` is the `f = (z + ·)` instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.combo_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.combo_mem","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L90-L93","doc":"A strict convex combination lies weakly between its endpoints. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.combo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.combo","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L87-L88","doc":"A strict convex combination, as in `PnBetweennessBlocksSignMixed`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.not_strict_max_of_monotone'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.not_strict_max_of_monotone'","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L74-L79","doc":"**The same, with the endpoints in the other order.** Betweenness is\nsymmetric; the exclusion should not depend on which like-pair letter is larger. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.not_strict_max_of_antitone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.not_strict_max_of_antitone","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L67-L72","doc":"**And so does an antitone one.** Reversing the order reverses which endpoint\ndoes the work, and the conclusion is unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.not_strict_max_of_monotone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceMonotone.not_strict_max_of_monotone","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceMonotoneBlocksSignMixed.lean#L60-L65","doc":"**A monotone map keeps the middle in the middle.** If `c` lies between `a`\nand `b` then `f c` does not strictly exceed both endpoints. ","signatureChunk":0}]}